    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 2567: Minimum Score by Changing Two Elements (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a 0-indexed integer array nums. The low score of nums is the minimum value of
                |nums[i] - nums[j]| over all 0 &lt;= i &lt; j &lt; nums.length. The high score of nums is the maximum
                value of |nums[i] - nums[j]| over all 0 &lt;= i &lt; j &lt; nums.length. The score of nums is the
                sum of the high and low scores of nums. To minimize the score of nums, we can change the
                value of at most two elements of nums. Return the minimum possible score after changing at
                most two elements of nums.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [1,4,7,8,5]<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: Change nums[0] and nums[1] to be 6, so nums becomes [6,6,7,8,5]. The low score
                is 0, since the first two elements are equal, and the high score is 3, so the score is
                0 + 3 = 3. It can be shown that no smaller score is achievable.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minimizeSum(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
        int hi1 = INT_MIN, hi2 = INT_MIN, hi3 = INT_MIN;
        int lo1 = INT_MAX, lo2 = INT_MAX, lo3 = INT_MAX;

        for (int x : nums) {
            if (x &gt; hi1) {
                hi3 = hi2;
                hi2 = hi1;
                hi1 = x;
            } else if (x &gt; hi2) {
                hi3 = hi2;
                hi2 = x;
            } else if (x &gt; hi3) {
                hi3 = x;
            }

            if (x &lt; lo1) {
                lo3 = lo2;
                lo2 = lo1;
                lo1 = x;
            } else if (x &lt; lo2) {
                lo3 = lo2;
                lo2 = x;
            } else if (x &lt; lo3) {
                lo3 = x;
            }
        }

        int res1 = hi3 - lo1;
        int res2 = hi2 - lo2;
        int res3 = hi1 - lo3;

        return min({res1, res2, res3});
    }
};</code></pre>
